<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mansĭto</span></b> , 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq. n.</i>
			[maneo], <i>to stay, remain, tarry, abide, dwell</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pygargus in oppidis mansitat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 3, 3, § 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sub eodem tecto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">una,</span>”
				<i>to pass the night</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 13, 44</span></i>
			; cf. maneo, B.; mansio, B. 1.</div>
